WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
Do you manage your time or do you manage your energy?

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.640
There's a profound difference.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:13.960
The most effective leaders are masters of energy management.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:18.600
This directly impacts your cognitive performance.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:24.320
Neuroscience shows that physical conditioning through things like aerobic training,

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.400
actually boost gray matter and executive function,

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.680
improving your focus, emotional regulation and discipline.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.537
Your physical wellness is the engine for

00:00:36.537 --> 00:00:39.680
your mental clarity and performance stamina.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.568
And with that understanding,

00:00:41.568 --> 00:00:45.680
they intentionally schedule their days not just around tasks,

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.240
but around their energy cycles.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:51.200
This is what separates high performers.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.019
I know a female executive who blocks the

00:00:54.019 --> 00:00:57.120
first 90 minutes of every day for deep work.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.600
No emails, no meetings.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:05.200
She also schedules two 15-minute recovery blocks in the afternoon.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:12.000
By managing her energy, she accomplishes more in six hours than most do in 10.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.720
Your play is to conduct a personal energy audit.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:23.920
For one day this week, I want you to track your energy levels, high, medium, low.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:30.720
In your playbook, note what activities drain you and what activities fuel you.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:36.480
You've identified that back-to-back meetings are your biggest energy drain.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.157
What is the one specific boundary you can set

00:01:40.157 --> 00:01:44.160
next week to protect your energy and performance?

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.604
In what ways are you protecting boundaries in your

00:01:47.604 --> 00:01:51.600
personal and professional life to create time of recovery?

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.880
To put this into practice, turn to the boundary setting drill in your playbook

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:00.560
and commit to one specific action.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.640
Once you've audited your energy,

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.800
we'll talk about how your habits impact your team's performance.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:10.000
I'll see you in the next video.
